## Implemented local outcome

Five sibling modules under `v2/experiments/action_executor/r27/pre_stage` reuse
unchanged original source and writer algorithms; two exact AST deltas configure
PRE codec subtype selection and its writer emit variant. No old HTTP contract,
epoch, framing, implementation, product or test source was edited.

| Scope | Main acceptance |
|---|---|
| G1 | Canonical typed PRE policy is consumed by codec/writer/recovery; distinct epoch and source/stage witnesses; closed per-path whole-write/count/metadata/aggregate checks precede destructive I/O. Same 20 wire families and shared 10MiB, without refunds. |
| G2 | Entire unchanged original corruption method, rows/write_packet and genuine unittest assertions execute through private logical I/O and original read validators/oracles. |
| G3 | Every synthetic frame has exactly one file owner; whole overwrite ranges, nine tombstones and six directory events are retained and checked. Paired recovery rejects role/count/history/cross-stage corruption. |
| G4 | Exact 33 unique outer groups pass; five-file health, complete source preservation, actual failure history and independent review agree. |
| G5 | Original PRE remains predispatch DENY; all unqualified native/platform routes are explicit. No expanded execution authority. |

### Genuine source sequence, not measured performance

The original method constructs 1,600 synthetic rows and writes the whole JSON
235,440B and whole JSONL 233,840B without splitting. It checks full PASS, eight
mutation/restoration integrity failures, journal truncation with no observed
count, four-row FAIL, and missing-summary reconstruction (observed 4/missing 1,596).

Actual sequence: **35 whole writes / 733,169B lifetime payload**. Before cleanup,
4,050B remains live. The source deletes its summary; owned cleanup deletes eight
remaining files and four directories deepest-first. All nine file tombstones,
two original mkdir calls and four rmdir calls remain in recovery metadata.
Deleted/overwritten bytes are still charged and retained in packet history.

| Bound | Bytes |
|---|---:|
| Actual shared charge, including closure | 1,532,954 |
| Closed per-path Cartesian payload maximum | 1,201,440 |
| Closed packet + physical + reserves maximum | 2,469,496 |
| Coarse codec-only ceiling (not a physical-copy proof) | 8,241,689 |
| Unchanged aggregate cap | 10,485,760 |

The local metadata reserve is explicitly adopted at 64KiB, inside the same cap.
Outer safety ceilings remain 32 entries/64 directories/64 tombstones, with the
stronger closed nine-path/35-call policy. Original HTTP metadata policy is unchanged.
Synthetic elapsed_ms=1.0 and process fixture fields are oracle inputs, not observed
HTTP/process performance. Original setUp and the six-test suite were not run.

