Source/preservation before and after are equal; scratch [] → [].
Public recovery controls include direct semantic-role mutations and actual sealed
manifest/packet/owner corruption, extra native file and missing seal, followed by
exact restoration and valid recovery. Post-seal tampering is an adversarial test,
not an admitted producer write.

Two disabled-plugin config warnings remain. Initial four type errors and source
snapshots are retained. Initial combined command yielded 22 pass/11 environment
failures (seven sandbox IPC denials, four missing backend imports); its returned
output was tool-truncated and is not represented as complete raw JSON. Corrected
clean environment/approved finite IPC ran the same source without changes.
Initial plugin-autoload warnings are disclosed. Local environment correction is
not a failed campaign retry. Main's initial display compared JS object identity;
deep content comparison immediately confirmed equality, with raw evidence intact.

## Authority and remaining boundary

Supported frozen `checks.py` validates new binding/evidence before effectful
derived imports and controlled workloads. Pure stage policy definitions load
before that gate. The diagnostic factory verifies old pins, scope and contract,
then snapshots current new-code witnesses: it is NOT standalone authorization
for arbitrary changed new code. Bare private codec/internal reflective access is
not a universal filesystem sandbox; accepted scope is the cooperative owned port.

Known original launcher 125 names + suite 14 names = 139 is an uncovered lower
bound, not an admitted full PRE domain. Genuine tempfile probe/fallback/rmtree,
pytest basetemp/current-symlink, shell/native outputs and unknown plugin/platform/
failure routes remain UNQUALIFIED/default DENY. Owned four-directory cleanup here
does not qualify stdlib TemporaryDirectory cleanup.

Next finite integration boundary is **genuine source-bound temporary-file creation,
probe/fallback/cleanup and pytest basetemp lifecycle, including failure paths**,
before wider PRE. No automatic campaign or executor activation follows. Missing
dependencies, Linux/physical SQL qualification and measured tail repair remain
separate prerequisites and authority boundaries.

69GiB free at finish; no whole-project copy, install, venv, build/distDir, tool cache
or Docker resource created. Exact owned test roots auto-cleaned, including failures;
no unrelated data was removed. Four previous current publications remain byte-exact.

